# Private runtime file: populate with the application's reviewed configuration.
# Do not copy a host .env blindly: hosts, paths and provider policies differ.
ITSM_INTERNAL_JOB_TOKEN=
HUB_MODEL_KEY=
MODEL_PROFILES=
# Copy all required specialist-key/provider/policy settings from your reviewed
# deployment configuration, using container paths and actual reachable hosts.
# Per-account outbound provider connections remain encrypted in extension state.
# The configured Hub is still warmed at startup; selecting an outbound model
# for an account does not make this a weightless AI service.
# If selecting the SQLite asset provider, set an explicit writable path such as
# ASSET_SQLITE_PATH=/state/assets/inventory.sqlite3. Provider selection is opt-in.
# DNS integrity check (defaults shown; a public resolver and its DNS-over-HTTPS address):
# DNS_CHECK_RESOLVER=1.1.1.1
# DNS_CHECK_DOH_URL=https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query
# DNS_CHECK_NAMES=example.com,wikipedia.org,github.com
# Independent read steps of one request that may run at the same time (1 or 2;
# default 1). Mutations always run alone; local models still take turns on the GPU.
# MAX_PARALLEL_SPECIALISTS=2
# Continual control state/capture paths and mailbox locks are supplied under
# /state by Compose. This does not enable learning or provide a mailbox server.
